    <DataNode elementId="CPD-7989" textLabel="(+)-valencene" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="QEBNYNLSCGVZOH-NFAWXSAZSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="540" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xu">(+)-Valencene is a natural bicyclic sesquiterpene that is found in various citrus species, such as the Valencia orange (|FRAME: TAX-2711|) |CITS: [Hunter65][ 24910970]|. Beside being an aroma compound, it possesses a variety of biological activities. It is produced from |FRAME: FARNESYL-PP| by |FRAME: EC-4.2.3.73| |CITS: [15464152]|.</Comment>
